1
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:04,600
This is Nova Wheels.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,067
Not a rental counter...

3
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:07,167
not a spreadsheet.

4
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:11,200
A complete system, built to make your fleet look like this.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,667
And run like this.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,200
Your customers land here first.

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:22,667
Every car, every rate, every rule, presented the way a Porsche or Lamborghini showroom would present it.

8
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:30,133
It opens with a cinematic reveal, the menu moves like a luxury app, and every page glides.

9
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:31,900
Because the first impression...

10
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,200
sets the price.

11
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:43,033
Each vehicle gets its own page.

12
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:43,500
Specs.

13
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,767
Daily, weekly and monthly rates.

14
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:49,833
Included miles, the deposit, all of it up front.

15
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:53,433
So renters stop asking questions, and start booking.

16
00:00:54,033 --> 00:00:55,567
Booking takes four screens.

17
00:00:55,567 --> 00:00:56,333
Which car.

18
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:58,633
Which dates, with a live estimate.

19
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:00,167
How to reach them.

20
00:01:00,167 --> 00:01:00,567
Done.

21
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:05,567
The request lands in your dashboard, with a name and a number attached.

22
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:11,233
Now, the part your customers never see.

23
00:01:11,233 --> 00:01:12,000
Your operation.

24
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,767
Sign in, and the first time through, it sets itself up like a new phone.

25
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:18,533
Your company.

26
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:19,300
Your lot.

27
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,467
Your house rules.

28
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:22,000
How you take money.

29
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,933
Eight questions, and you're live.

30
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:26,067
Every morning starts here.

31
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:26,833
What's out.

32
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:27,967
What's due back.

33
00:01:27,967 --> 00:01:29,100
Who owes you.

34
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,000
What still needs a signature.

35
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:31,767
One screen.

36
00:01:31,767 --> 00:01:32,533
No digging.

37
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,733
And this is the heart of it.

38
00:01:35,733 --> 00:01:36,800
Handle a rental.

39
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,233
One question per screen.

40
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:38,967
Which car?

41
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:40,767
Pick it from the fleet.

42
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:45,100
Or if it's brand new, type the VIN, and it decodes itself.

43
00:01:45,733 --> 00:01:51,167
Odometer, fuel, every pre-existing mark, photographed and timestamped before the keys move.

44
00:01:51,167 --> 00:01:52,533
Then the renter.

45
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:53,000
Name.

46
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:53,467
Contact.

47
00:01:53,467 --> 00:01:57,100
License, with an age gate for every car.

48
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:58,900
An address that autocompletes.

49
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:01,633
Insurance you verify on the spot.

50
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:05,700
If they've rented before, one tap pulls their file.

51
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,967
And if they're flagged do-not-rent...

52
00:02:07,967 --> 00:02:10,233
the system stops you cold.

53
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:11,967
Then, the money.

54
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:15,800
Term, rate, mileage, deposit, down payment, and how they pay.

55
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:25,000
Card on file is the default, because it's the only method that lets you recover tolls, tickets and damage after the car is back.

56
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,733
Pick Zelle or cash, and it warns you, and still requires a card for incidentals.

57
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:33,400
That is the difference between a business...

58
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,533
and a hobby.

59
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:38,533
Every answer flows straight into the contract.

60
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:41,867
Eighteen clauses written to protect the owner.

61
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:42,833
Late returns.

62
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:43,800
Prohibited use.

63
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,767
GPS consent.

64
00:02:44,767 --> 00:02:46,200
Loss of use.

65
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,167
Chargeback language.

66
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:54,800
And under each one, a plain-English line, so the renter can never say they didn't understand.

67
00:02:55,367 --> 00:02:59,133
Sign right there on the screen, or send a link.

68
00:02:59,133 --> 00:03:04,033
On their phone, they initial each money clause, read the rules, and sign.

69
00:03:04,033 --> 00:03:07,800
You get a timestamp, their device, and a countersign button.

70
00:03:08,467 --> 00:03:12,167
When the car comes back, check-in does the math.

71
00:03:12,167 --> 00:03:13,000
Miles over.

72
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,833
Fuel short.

73
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:14,667
Hours late.

74
00:03:14,667 --> 00:03:15,500
Cleaning, smoking.

75
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,367
All computed and itemized against the deposit.

76
00:03:18,367 --> 00:03:24,533
GPS and starter interrupt live right on the rental, with a log of every action.

77
00:03:24,533 --> 00:03:25,367
And payments...

78
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:29,467
every installment, every deduction, across every rental, in one ledger.

79
00:03:29,467 --> 00:03:36,867
So when it's time to talk to a bank, or apply for funding, your numbers are already organized.

80
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,500
So what does this actually do for the business?

81
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:44,167
It lets customers book from the website, instead of your DMs.

82
00:03:44,167 --> 00:03:48,500
It makes you look like a brand people expect to pay more for.

83
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,833
It puts every dollar in writing before the keys move.

84
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:56,167
And it turns a stack of paperwork into six minutes on a screen.

85
00:03:56,167 --> 00:03:56,833
Nova Wheels.

86
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:58,500
Let's put it to work.

